-- emit/release: `backend.md` §9 item 1's zero-use rule after its
-- 2026-09-30 amendment — a binding nothing reads is dropped whole when its
-- right-hand side is pure, and kept, evaluated for its effect, when it may
-- be impure or may suspend (`language.md` §6, *What an optimiser may
-- assume*). Running a program shows the kept half (`run/ReleaseKeepsNamed*`);
-- only the bytes can show the dropped half, so it is goldened here.
--
-- In `keep`, nothing reads `quiet`, `measured` or `started`:
--
--   - `quiet` is arithmetic and `measured` a chain of pure calls: both are
--     GONE from the golden, initialiser and all;
--   - `started` calls `Task.spawn`, a `foreign impure`: its `const` stays,
--     name and all, although nothing reads it.
import String
import Task


pub keep : Int -> Int
keep n =
    quiet = n * 1000
    measured = String.length (String.fromInt n)
    started = Task.spawn λ() -> n
    n
